      "text": "End-bent backwall, cheek-wall and tie-back strap calculation added to the journal (task T017) as EndBentBackwallDesign, the Blockpad edition of the 19 October 2026 notebook case (D-057: report Backwall Design 10-19.html, SHA-256 6ed9ebb7bd2d…; case SHA-256 01e76c5a263a…). The notebook package was reconciled with the register (End Bent 1_Fixed.XML of D-049 with the D-051 case that records it; the D-053/D-055 CAD model measured natively: two planar 2% backwall tops 4.25 in below the deck-top line, crown 4.0691 ft and edges 3.8733 ft above the cap top, backwall volume 77.770 ft3, landing tributary length 17.155 ft; the T016 journal) and rerun: bearing actions unchanged, strap loads 3.089 kip/ft service and 3.737 kip/ft factored (16 October: 3.094 / 3.746), all numerical checks pass, nine check entries pending across the six unconfirmed prerequisites (settlement, strap elevation, exposure, shrinkage, analysis confirmation, cheek anchorage); decisions D-014 to D-019 unchanged. In the journal edition the end-bent cap, backwall thickness, cheek thickness, pedestal, bearing pad and Span 1 values are live references to Bridge Geometry, the material strengths to Materials and the project stamp to ProjectInfo (23 references, each equal to the case; the bearing spacing stays the 102.99-in analysis value against the 103-in journal beam spacing); drop_bw references EndBent_backwallDrop beside the measured heights. Indexed in PedBridge; Bridge Geometry and Foundation Modeling name the report. Distilled numerical checks only, not design acceptance; native recalculation not performed; FBMP not rerun.",
